---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "BacTermFinder - Scholaraize";
const description = "A comprehensive ensemble of Convolutional Neural Networks for identifying both intrinsic and factor-dependent transcription terminators.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-16">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 bg-primary/10 text-primary rounded-full text-sm mb-6">
          <span>⭐</span>
          <span>Featured Project</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-6 text-slate-900">
          BacTermFinder
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          A comprehensive ensemble of Convolutional Neural Networks for identifying both intrinsic and factor-dependent transcription terminators.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4 justify-center">
          <a href="/projects/bactermfinder/app" class="btn-primary">
            EXPLORE
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/BioinformaticsLabAtMUN/BacTermFinder" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-secondary">
            GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="card mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">Background</h2>
          <div class="prose prose-lg">
            <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
              Transcription is the process of synthesizing RNA from a DNA template. It begins at the promoter and ends at the Terminator, a specific DNA segment that signals the RNA polymerase to stop.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
              Accurately identifying these terminators is crucial for understanding operon structures and gene regulation. However, existing computational tools are often specialized for specific bacteria or specific terminator types, lacking a truly general solution.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-600">
              BacTermFinder bridges this gap. By training on over 41,000 terminators from 22 diverse bacterial species with GC content ranging from 28% to 71%, it provides a general-purpose model capable of detecting multiple terminator types with high accuracy.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">The Biology</h2>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-slate-900">Intrinsic Terminators</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-3">
                Characterized by a distinct "hairpin" structure in the RNA transcript. This forms due to a GC-rich region followed by a poly-thymine (poly-U in RNA) sequence. The weak base pairing allows the transcript to detach, terminating transcription.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-slate-900">Factor-Dependent Terminators</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-3">
                More complex, requiring both cis-acting RNA elements and proteins like Rho to halt transcription. The Rho utilization (rut) site is typically 60–90 nucleotides upstream of the terminator.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">The CNN Ensemble</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
            BacTermFinder processes DNA through four independent CNNs, each trained on different sequence representations, then averages their predictions.
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
            <div class="bg-slate-100 rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
              <span class="text-2xl mb-2 block">📊</span>
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm text-slate-900">PS2</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Pseudo-Dinucleotide</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-100 rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
              <span class="text-2xl mb-2 block">📈</span>
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm text-slate-900">ENAC</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Spatial Location</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-100 rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
              <span class="text-2xl mb-2 block">🔢</span>
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm text-slate-900">One-Hot</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Binary Encoding</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-100 rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
              <span class="text-2xl mb-2 block">⚗️</span>
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm text-slate-900">NCP</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">Chemical Properties</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">Performance</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
            BacTermFinder outperforms all other approaches in terms of average recall without increasing the number of false positives.
          </p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-200">
                  <th class="text-left py-2 px-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">Tool</th>
                  <th class="text-center py-2 px-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">Mean Recall</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-100">
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-slate-900 font-semibold">BacTermFinder</td>
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-center text-primary font-bold">0.57</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-100">
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-slate-600">TermNN</td>
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-center text-slate-600">0.46</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-100">
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-slate-600">TransTermHP</td>
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-center text-slate-600">0.25</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-100">
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-slate-600">RhoTermPredict</td>
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-center text-slate-600">0.15</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-slate-600">ITerm-PseKNC</td>
                  <td class="py-2 px-4 text-center text-slate-600">0.13</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">Impact</h2>
          <div class="prose prose-lg">
            <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
              One of the most striking results is BacTermFinder's ability to generalize. It successfully identifies terminators in Archaea, even though it was trained exclusively on Bacterial data.
            </p>
            <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
              With an average recall of 0.57 ± 0.21 on independent validation sets, BacTermFinder sets a new standard for genome-wide terminator prediction, aiding in the annotation of new genomes and the design of synthetic genetic circuits.
            </p>
            <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-primary pl-4 italic text-slate-600">
              "BacTermFinder outperforms all other four approaches in terms of average recall without increasing the number of false positives."
              <footer class="text-sm mt-2 text-slate-500">— Taheri Ghahfarokhi & Peña-Castillo (2025)</footer>
            </blockquote>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">Research Team</h2>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="bg-slate-100 rounded-lg p-4">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Seyed Mohammad Amin Taheri Ghahfarokhi</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Memorial University of Newfoundland</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-100 rounded-lg p-4">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Lourdes Peña-Castillo</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Memorial University of Newfoundland</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-4">Department of Computer Science & Department of Biology, Memorial University of Newfoundland.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">Publication</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 mb-2">
            Taheri Ghahfarokhi, S. M. A., & Peña-Castillo, L. (2025). BacTermFinder: a comprehensive and general bacterial terminator finder using a CNN ensemble. NAR Genomics and Bioinformatics, 7(1), lqaf016.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-primary">
            DOI: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1093/nargab/lqaf016" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">10.1093/nargab/lqaf016</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
